The files in programs/pascal/ are the Pascal-P4 portable Pascal compiler
and interpreter, originally written at:

  Institut fuer Informatik, Eidgenoessische Technische Hochschule (ETH)
  CH-8096 Zuerich

  pcom.pas  - compiler, by Urs Ammann, Kesav Nori, and Christian Jacobi
  pint.pas  - P-code assembler/interpreter, credited to
              K. Jensen, N. Wirth, and Ch. Jacobi (ETH, May 1976)

This code is documented in:

  Steven Pemberton and Martin Daniels, "Pascal Implementation"
  Ellis Horwood, Chichester, UK, 1982 (ISBN 0-13-653-0311)

Pascal-P4 was distributed by ETH as a portable implementation kit intended
to be copied, ported, and modified. The copy here is the Free Pascal / Delphi
port by Christophe Staiesse (2013); the lex/yacc grammar in programs/pascal/
grammar/ carries an MIT license. These files are included for reference,
testing, and educational purposes. The CC0 dedication in LICENSE applies to
original contributions in this repository; it does not retroactively affect
the copyright status of the original ETH Pascal-P4 sources.

